    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "deployment watcher raft shim server", "note": "located deploymentWatcherRaftShim (deployment_watcher_shims.go:13), DeploymentRaftEndpoints (deployments_watcher.go:40), and setupDeploymentWatcher (server.go:1156), all cited"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "RPCHandler (file client/config/config.go)", "note": "correctly showed nomad.Server satisfies the interface and config.Config composes it, anchoring the latent client route"}
  ],
  "q1_wrong": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "note": "retained_via_interfaces rows for client-side RPCer holders (allocrunner, allocwatcher, widmgr) implied server retention, but grep showed Config.RPCHandler is never assigned in production — those hold *client.Client; also stream.EventBroker appeared as a Server caller but has no retaining field (verified by reading event_broker.go:29-45)"}
  ],
  "q2_fallbacks": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "exact line numbers of the retaining FIELDS (e.g. srv *Server at rpc.go:48, encrypter at auth/auth.go:64, raft at drainer.go:159) — blast gives struct line ranges, not field declarations"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "runtime wiring proof for interface rows: who assigns the shim/endpoint into the field (server.go:1160, 1180, 1189, worker.go:628) had to be recovered with grep/read"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "RPCHandler (file client/config/config.go)", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "no evidence of where the field is ASSIGNED; grep for 'RPCHandler =' revealed it is never set in production, which flipped the audit conclusion"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "nomad.Server", "fallback": "read", "missing": "closure/method-value retention (auth StateFn=s.State, shim apply=s.raftApply) — index_caveat admits function-value passing is missed; found only by reading server.go:475-483 and the shim files"}
  ],
  "q3_hints": [
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query_before": "nomad.Server (graph)", "query_after": "nomad.Server (blast)", "hint": "next_steps: '51 callers reach this - run sense_blast for full change impact and what holds it (retained_via_interfaces, holders that keep it behind an interface and never name it)' — I had queued blast in parallel, and the retained_note in its output ('unverified... which satisfier the field holds at runtime') directly caused my grep verification of the client-side RPCer rows"}
  ],
  "q4_value": "retained_via_interfaces on sense_blast: a ready-made list of holders whose fields never name *Server (Planner→Worker, RaftApplier→drainerShim, CSIVolumeRPC, JobEvalDispatcher, auth.Encrypter) — exactly the easy-to-miss class the ticket was about, delivered in one call.",
  "q5_improve": "For each retained_via_interfaces row, include the exact field declaration line and the assignment site(s) where the interface value is constructed (e.g. server.go:1189 drainerShim{s}), so the runtime-binding trace doesn't require a grep/read pass per route.",
  "score": 9,
  "score_rationale": "Q1 shows blast/graph delivered the transitive interface-retention set (23 rows) and the complete composed_by holder list in two calls — not recoverable by grep in this session at that completeness — while Q1-wrong/Q2 fallbacks were verification and field-line refinement, not wrong locations."
}

